  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating outcomes with probability less than 20% and increasing their weight by 10 percentage points, then comparing the weighted sums. However, in this problem, no outcome has a probability below 20%. The 20% outcome in Lottery B is not below 20%, so it is not subject to the adjustment. Therefore, the decision reason is not triggered. The individual's reasoning, which emphasizes that losing has no effect ('nothing happens when you lose'), does not involve any weighting of outcomes or any calculation based on adjusted probabilities. Instead, it reflects a different psychological or behavioral principle — the irrelevance of losses — which is unrelated to the decision reason. Since the individual neither considers the relevant outcomes (which don’t exist under the rule) nor applies the rule’s weighting mechanism, the decision reason was not used. The reasoning is conceptually and procedurally distinct from the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
